mantle rm345
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rmx_millicent_wickwick
title the carter's straw skirts
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=carter temper=calm
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk tucks_straw_pads_under_anything_that_rattles
likes oatcakes dice fresh_straw summer_evenings
dislikes deep_mud stale_bread
fears a_pot_bouncing_over_the_rim a_back_wheel_sinking
hopes a_summer_route_with_room_to_stop_for_supper
topics travel +0.5 work +0.5 food +0.3 weather +0.2 pastimes +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=plain refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# tucks pads of straw around noisy parcels, takes stairs in pairs to catch a load before it shifts, and enjoys a journey best when there is just one small thing to deliver.

words
oath! = Axle and awning | Rattle my skirts
saying! = Straw weighs less than a broken pot | A slow wheel leaves a whole supper
skirt = a skirt of twisted straw | my straw wrapping
hollow = a soft nest | a hollow in the packing
wheelmark = a shining strip of rim | a wheel's dark tread
twist = a handful of straw turned under | a flat straw twist
oatround = my round oatcake | a small buttered oatcake
bucketear = the eye of a bucket handle | a little handle ring
uphill = the pull towards the crest | the last piece of the climb
mudhole = the middle of a soft rut | a stretch of churned clay
loadsong = the soft run of the load | a quiet roll of wood
diecorner = a rounded dice corner | the small edge of a die
settle = a little settling noise | one low wooden sigh

any
opinion road for 2 : I like a road with enough life in it to ask for care and enough kindness to bring the load home.
opinion dole for 3 : I'd wedge another bowl in any cart before I'd leave a hungry wolf standing there.
opinion church for 1 : A prayer can travel wedged between quite ordinary thoughts about the road. The Bright One finds it easily.
opinion strangers for 1 : A new face on a long stretch can make the next turn worth seeing.
opinion merchants against 1 : A price set for carrying ought to stay the same when the last crate comes out.
opinion houses against 1 : I've seen a crest given a comfortable ride on a wagon that badly wanted mending.
opinion times against 1 : It seems to take a longer road each week to earn the same oatcake.

grown
line greet : Come where you won't catch a sleeve on the straw.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A little room left for company. Welcome to it.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning light, quiet wheels. Good time to meet.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : The evening's still wide enough to share.
line greet.return : A word from the roadside does my ears good.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Good! I'd recognise that voice through four loose buckets.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : There's room for talk if there's room to turn round.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : I had nearly missed your voice in the dark there.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Take the comfortable bit. Family saves trouble that way.
line again.open : I kept your last words good and snug.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Hoy there, travelling friend! Level with my elbow.
line farewell : Go lightly over the places that shake.
line farewell.return : And let the last turn bring you somewhere pleasant.
line react.news : Let me hear what travelled in with you.
line react.news.new : Not a wheel of that has rolled past my hearing.
line react.news.known : That same load of news came by me earlier.
line react.news.doubt : Something's knocking loose beneath that account.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Poor wolf. I wish some ordinary comfort could reach there.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Glad news will ride with me quite willingly.
line ask.how : Has the way been easy underfoot?
line answer.how : I've had more jolts than bruises. A fair return.
line thank : That's one less corner for me to worry over.
line deflect_thanks : It was no more weight than a twist of straw.
line sympathise : Lean on this till you feel the ground again.
line reassure : Let the jolt finish travelling through you. I'll wait.
line decline : I'd gladly help once my present load is safely down.
line accept_decline : Then fit the hour to your own errands.
line preclose : I mean to arrive with daylight to spare.
line accept_preclose : Here's hoping a shaded road takes you home.

scene quiet_skirt
when topic=work|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two empty pots can make more din than a whole marriage feast. | You can hear the load settle if you leave it a moment.
b : How do you quiet the pair? | What does settled sound like?
a : #skirt.capitalize# round each belly. They can touch without quarrelling. | Like a wooden sigh that doesn't need an answer.

scene why_two
when topic=pastimes|travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take stairs by twos only when my hands are empty. | A good stride can save a jar that's rolling loose.
b : In a hurry to go up? | You've raced jars?
a : In a hurry to come down where I'm wanted. | Jars go faster than you think and corner poorly.

scene keep_team
when topic=work self.job=carter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a load a moment after the first pull. | On an uphill turn I listen for one rattle growing louder.
b : Checking the team? | And if it does?
a : Checking the load first. The team can feel its own balance better than it can feel a crate's. | Ease off, pack the loose thing, start again. A small stop for a whole delivery.

scene oatpad
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #oatround.capitalize# wraps comfortably in the heel of my paw. | I like a little butter on a travelling oatcake.
b : Doesn't it crumble? | For flavour?
a : I start round the rim and nibble like a very deliberate mouse. | Helps the stray crumbs stick to supper instead of to my coat.

scene straw_room
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The nicest bit of straw is just off the top, where the dusty ends haven't settled. | I can twist a pad thick enough for a whole pot with one hand.
b : For bedding? | What occupies the other hand?
a : For anybody I've invited to sit a moment. | Generally the pot. One day I'll have the foresight to set it down.

scene dice_mat
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Dice like level ground even more than a wheel does. | Roll on a fold of cloth and a throw stays among friends.
b : Which bit runs truly level? | Trouble with runaway dice?
a : Let one die run. If it comes home it wasn't level. | I've had more exercise off one six than off some whole games.

scene summering
when topic=season here.season=summer
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : A long summer evening leaves time for the shadows to catch the cart. | Light stays beyond a high wall when my side's gone grey.
b : Do you wait for them? | Like having a spare evening.
a : I eat an oatcake and give them a sporting chance. | Exactly. I take the road which spends it last.

scene stale_bread
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A heel of bread shouldn't knock back when you rap a board with it. | I'd sooner pack the cart with yesterday's loaf than try and chew through it.
b : Beyond saving? | Wouldn't that waste a supper?
a : There's usually a soup pot with an open mind about such things. | Good point. Soup gets the first bid.

scene mud_course
when topic=weather|travel self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : That slim dry strip between two wheel tracks is generally wishful thinking. | #mudhole.capitalize# takes a good impression of everything but good manners.
b : Whose wish? | Did it swallow your boot?
a : Mine. I poke it before I trust a wheel to it. | Tried. We parted with some words neither of us meant.

scene works_bell
when topic=home self.quarter=works
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Around the Works you can tell how full the street is by the beat after the bell. | I like looking back from the Works at a city still lit above the smoke.
b : Boots all together? | Why look back?
a : First a great trampling, then a late pair hurrying along behind. | A job can fill the whole day. I enjoy being reminded there's a rest of the city.

scene mother_parcel
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd pad a parcel for #self.mother# with the sweetest straw I could buy. | For #self.mother# I'd bring an oatcake home whole.
b : Won't good straw be quite enough? | That's hard on a hungry road.
a : Probably. Sweet straw would say something I mightn't get out of my mouth. | I'd buy two and answer the difficulty at once.

scene dear_load
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A light cart can land heavily on an empty purse. | I stretch #twist# out longer in a lean week.
b : There's less to carry? | Can a bit of packing matter?
a : Less to be paid for at journey's end. | A cracked dish matters plenty to the wolf who can't buy a second one.

scene cart_late
when topic=travel|times world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A road looks oddly broad whenever a wagon's overdue. | I wish I could send spare patience to a delayed cart the way I send spare straw.
b : Because you're watching it? | Wouldn't that be useful here instead?
a : Yes. Every wagon-shaped gap suddenly has my eye. | Half the bundle for each, if you like.

scene arrival_name
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A newcomer deserves to know which way the slippery cobbles run. | I give directions from a place you'd be glad to get back to.
b : Can anybody slip correctly? | Why start there?
a : Preferably none. A little warning comes cheaper than a new pot. | Makes a wrong turn feel less final.

scene road_account
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : #world.news#. The place I got with it was #world.news_from#. | This travelled under the name of #world.news_from#: #world.news#.
b : How did it strike you? | Could there be another bit?
a : As a thing worth carrying in the state it reached me. | If there is, it's still on its way. My load stops here.

scene loose_tongue
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. It's the account I heard and no more. | Word round here is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I can't swear to the road it took.
b : Can it ride farther? | You're careful what you carry.
a : It can, if you keep my doubts packed beside it. | Names don't come with straw skirts to protect them.

scene short_errand
when topic=dreams|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like one whole day with nothing to deliver but a single ripe plum. | My most pleasant road would end before my lunch got cold.
b : A whole cart for one plum? | Rather a short road.
a : Give everybody I met a little imaginary lift. | Good. Plenty of time to cook another lunch.

scene bucket_breath
when topic=pastimes|work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can tell an empty bucket's complaint from the complaint of a lid. | Tap #bucketear# gently and the handle answers.
b : Which is louder? | What can you learn from it?
a : A lid, if you give the bucket a vote. | Whether it wants a twist of straw or a visit to a proper smith.

story wrapped_cake [topic=food|memories]
  : Once I packed my lunch between two very tidy pads of straw.
  : Opened the bundle and found a perfect straw picture pressed into the butter.
  b : Did you save the picture?
  : Ate the field from one corner right across. Best harvest I've ever had.

story road_nod [topic=travel|memories]
  : I nodded all morning to what I thought was a very patient wolf beside a gate.
  : Came back through in the evening and found a coat hung over a post.
  b : Did you feel foolish?
  : A little. Still gave it a nod in the evening. Good manners had cost me nothing so far.

story sack_sound [topic=work|memories self.job=carter]
  : Every sack on a particular run started singing on the same corner.
  : I dropped down to listen and couldn't get another note out of them.
  b : What ended the music?
  : My boot had a stone in the buckle. Half a cartload of innocent sacks were discharged at once.

rule @packing_edge
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two thin twists fit a corner better than one great fistful.

rule @warm_evening
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Good light enough to carry a little way inside.

rule @dusty_road
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's almost a tune in that quiet rattling.

rule @spread_straw
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Put the springy bit where the weight will come.

dlg resident.hub : I can make a comfortable corner for a few words.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. Good to have the company of that voice again.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : We can speak softly. Everything carries farther after dark.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : That's room enough for two civil voices at a distance.
dlg resident.job [self.job=carter] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I listen to the load as carefully as I look ahead.
dlg resident.job : I like to finish with everything in as good a shape as when it came to me.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The place on this account is #world.news_from#. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Take care of the name if you carry that farther.
dlg resident.bye : A comfortable ride to you, or a gentle walk if that's your portion.

graft resident.hub
choice Why wrap an empty pot as carefully as a full one? -> empty_shape
node empty_shape
say The one expecting delivery has bought all the space inside that pot. A crack can lose the space just as surely as it loses a dipperful of stew.
choice Do you listen for a crack? -> ring_and_wrap
choice I wouldn't want a broken space. -> hub
node ring_and_wrap
say Before I wrap it, I give the rim a light tap. One honest ring at this end, one honest ring when it's handed over.
choice I like the sound of that business. -> hub
choice May the next pot ring true. -> bye
